  "contents": "Does the Residential Tenancies Act, 2006 (Ontario) make this clause of a residential tenancy agreement void?\n\nRead the clause as a term of an ordinary private residential tenancy in Ontario that the Residential Tenancies Act, 2006 covers: the rental unit has no exemption under section 6.1, and it is not student housing, a care home, a co-operative or a mobile home park.\n\nYou are not given the text of the Act. Answer from what you know of it.\n\n<clause>\nThe Tenant shall pay for every repair to the unit during the tenancy, whatever the cause.\n</clause>\n\nAnswer with:\n- verdict: \"void\" if the Act makes the clause void, \"allowed\" if the Act permits it, or \"unsure\" if you can't decide.\n- section: the number of the one section that decides it, such as \"14\", without a subsection. Empty if unsure.\n- quote: the words of that section that decide it, exactly as they appear in the Act: one continuous passage from a single subsection, at least five words, with nothing left out, added or changed. Not a heading. Empty if unsure.\n- reason: one or two sentences.\n",
